## 2. FILE AND ROUTE ARCHITECTURE

### 2.1 Routing rules

TanStack Start file-based routing in `src/routes/`. Only root layout is `src/routes/__root.tsx`. Do not create `src/pages/`, `src/routes/_app/index.tsx`, or `app/layout.tsx`. Dynamic segments use bare `$`, e.g. `info.$slug.tsx`. `routeTree.gen.ts` is auto-generated; do not hand-edit.

`src/router.tsx`:

```ts
import { QueryClient } from "@tanstack/react-query";
import { createRouter } from "@tanstack/react-router";
import { routeTree } from "./routeTree.gen";

export const getRouter = () => {
  const queryClient = new QueryClient();
  const router = createRouter({
    routeTree,
    context: { queryClient },
    scrollRestoration: true,
    defaultPreloadStaleTime: 0,
  });
  return router;
};
```

### 2.2 11 static + 1 dynamic route = 19 URLs

Static: `/`, `/account`, `/careers`, `/checkout`, `/forgot-password`, `/login`, `/messages`, `/sellers`, `/shop`, `/signup`, `/support`.
Dynamic `/info/$slug`: `about`, `contact`, `shipping`, `returns`, `faq`, `privacy-terms`, `size`, `cookies`.

No `beforeLoad` guards exist. The only route-level redirect is an effect in `account.tsx`: signed-out → `/login`, seller → `/sellers`.

