## 8. SSR, SECURITY, ERROR HANDLING

### 8.1 src/start.ts

Defines `errorMiddleware` server middleware:
- Rethrows objects with `statusCode`.
- Others log and return 500 `text/html; charset=utf-8` from `renderErrorPage()`.
- Explicitly re-adds `createCsrfMiddleware({ filter: ctx => ctx.handlerType === "serverFn" })` because defining `src/start.ts` opts out of Start's automatic install.
- `startInstance = createStart(() => ({ requestMiddleware: [errorMiddleware, csrfMiddleware] }))`.

### 8.2 src/server.ts

- Lazy-caches `@tanstack/react-start/server-entry` import.
- `normalizeCatastrophicSsrResponse()` detects JSON `{"unhandled":true,"message":"HTTPError"}` on 5xx, returns 500 HTML with `cache-control: no-store`.
- Default export worker handler `{ fetch(request, env, ctx) }`: wraps handler, applies `normalizeCatastrophicSsrResponse`, then `applySecurityHeaders` on every response including errors.

### 8.3 src/lib/error-capture.ts

